Aim 
To implement a Queue using an Array and perform Enqueue and Dequeue operations using the C 
programming language. 
Procedure 
1. Start the program.  
2. Declare an array to represent the queue and initialize front and rear.  
3. Insert elements into the queue using the Enqueue operation.  
4. Display the queue.  
5. Remove one element using the Dequeue operation.  
6. Display the updated queue.  
7. Stop the program.   
Program 
#include <stdio.h> 
int main() 
{ 
    int queue[5], front = 0, rear = -1, i; 
    // Enqueue Operation 
    queue[++rear] = 10; 
    queue[++rear] = 20; 
    queue[++rear] = 30; 
 
    printf("Queue after Enqueue:\n"); 
    for(i = front; i <= rear; i++) 
    { 
        printf("%d ", queue[i]); 
    } 
    // Dequeue Operation 
    printf("\n\nDequeued Element = %d\n", queue[front]); 
    front++; 
 
    printf("\nQueue after Dequeue:\n"); 
    for(i = front; i <= rear; i++) 
    { 
        printf("%d ", queue[i]); 
    } 
 
    return 0; 
} 
Output 
Queue after Enqueue: 
10 20 30 
Dequeued Element = 10 
Queue after Dequeue: 
20 30 
Result 
Thus, a Queue was implemented successfully using an Array, and the Enqueue and Dequeue operations 
were performed using the C programming language.
